# voting-sim — agent rules

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root for layout, roadmap stage, and cleanup policy.

## Language & docs

- Code, comments, commits, agent docs: English.
- Do not rewrite `docs/ROADMAP.md` unless the user asks (it is Russian, human-facing).

## Scenes

- `Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity` is the **test/sandbox** scene — keep it.
- Polling-station greybox and future playable levels go in **new** scene assets under `Assets/Scenes/`.

## Skills — read `SKILL.md` before implementing

| Trigger                                 | Skill                                           |
| --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| Unity C# / MonoBehaviour                | `unity-csharp-scripting`                        |
| Input System / `.inputactions`          | `unity-input-system`                            |
| UI (unspecified)                        | `ui` then specialized                           |
| Canvas / uGUI                           | `ui-ugui`                                       |
| Physics / triggers / raycasts           | `physics-3d-collision`                          |
| Editor automation / scene edits via CLI | `unity-cli` (+ `unity-pipeline` if Editor open) |
| URP Volume / post-fx                    | `urp-postprocessing`                            |
| UPM packages                            | `unity-package-management`                      |

Ignore unrelated ecosystems (web, MAUI, Blazor, etc.).

## Git / assets

- Do not commit `Library/`, `Temp/`, `Logs/`, `UserSettings/`, build folders.
- Keep `.meta` paired with assets.
- Prefer Unity Editor / `unity-cli` for scene/prefab changes over large hand-edited YAML.
- Save all `.cs` (and other text sources) as **UTF-8** per `.editorconfig`. Do not use Windows-1251.
